00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:58.340
Here, I will read the letter entrusted
by His Majesty Utena Itsukinomiya Touri,

00:01:58.340 --> 00:02:01.590
my lord and the head of the Saiguu Family

00:02:01.590 --> 00:02:05.630
who holds the highest authority in Yamato.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:08.550
You should listen respectfully.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:07.130
Who's that again?

00:02:07.130 --> 00:02:08.550
Be quiet!

00:02:08.550 --> 00:02:10.550
"To the good and brave people

00:02:10.550 --> 00:02:14.500
who gathered in Akiba,
a famous Adventurers' town.

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:17.710
I hereby declare anew
that I place full confidence

00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:20.340
in Eins, whom I bestowed a title of duke,

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:24.460
as well as in the Akiba Government,
an organization he wishes to found,

00:02:24.460 --> 00:02:29.750
and that I will spare no effort to support them.

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:31.800
Eins sees the larger picture

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:35.590
and places thoughtful consideration
to every corner of the town.

00:02:35.590 --> 00:02:38.050
With his intelligence and kindness,

00:02:38.050 --> 00:02:43.170
I have no doubt that he
is suitable to lead this town."

00:02:43.170 --> 00:02:46.710
He understands what election speeches are.

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:49.630
He praises Eins so much that it's too much.

00:02:49.630 --> 00:02:52.630
Well, I'm not sure if it's too much.

00:02:52.630 --> 00:02:56.550
Those words are my honest thoughts.

00:02:56.550 --> 00:02:59.300
I believe in you, Eins.

00:02:59.650 --> 00:03:05.580
Blessings

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:03.460
"Blessings."

00:03:06.050 --> 00:03:09.630
"I imagine there are those who might fear that

00:03:09.630 --> 00:03:15.590
if the one I support wins,
this town may be affected by Westelande.

00:03:15.590 --> 00:03:21.670
However, I solemnly swear that I will
never let them unreasonably intervene.

00:03:21.670 --> 00:03:27.300
How will this battle
we call 'election' be settled?

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:24.630
I appreciate that pledge.

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:32.130
More than anything, I need people to
believe Akiba's independence is guaranteed.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:32.130
There is no way of knowing it; however,
our opponent is a worthy adversary.

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:34.340
The one who stands in our way

00:03:34.340 --> 00:03:42.000
is someone inscrutable and worthy
of being praised as the 'Geki in the East'."

00:03:36.880 --> 00:03:42.000
"Geki in the East"? What is "Geki"?

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:44.920
It probably means an upper-ranked official.

00:03:44.920 --> 00:03:47.050
I think he's talking about Shiro.

00:03:47.050 --> 00:03:50.880
Shiro must be considered a super incredible guy.

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:55.170
"This town is blessed with its people
and a geographical advantage.

00:03:55.170 --> 00:03:57.300
I congratulate its future.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:01.800
I hope this town will be an even more
comfortable place to live for everyone.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:06.420
With such prayers and blessings,
I finish my words."

00:04:13.500 --> 00:04:16.210
Prayers and blessings...

00:04:16.210 --> 00:04:19.550
Right... That must be it.

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:24.170
What this town needs right now is...

00:04:24.170 --> 00:04:26.880
I almost made a mistake.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.920
First, I was going to deny the raison d'etre
of the Round Table Conference.

00:04:29.920 --> 00:04:32.840
Then, I was going to promise
to improve their living.

00:04:32.840 --> 00:04:36.630
And then... And then...

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:42.210
But what they seek now definitely
aren't detailed explanations like that.

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.090
More hope...

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:49.880
Even if people call them empty words
and laugh at me, I should give them hope.

00:04:49.880 --> 00:04:54.300
Ladies and gentlemen. Akiba will improve more.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:58.590
Looking back, this town was too shorthanded.

00:04:58.590 --> 00:05:03.750
Despite that, we Adventurers
believed only in our abilities

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:07.380
and knew too little about
the People of the Land.

00:05:07.380 --> 00:05:12.170
On the other hand, I think the
People of the Land felt timid around us

00:05:12.170 --> 00:05:16.460
and didn't ask for our help often enough.

00:05:16.460 --> 00:05:18.840
This is the point that'll improve.

00:05:18.840 --> 00:05:23.800
We'll get a little better at helping each other.

00:05:23.800 --> 00:05:28.050
Those who want help won't be servile
and will appreciate the support.

00:05:28.050 --> 00:05:32.880
Those who give help won't be arrogant
and will be considerate to their neighbors.

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:35.670
Akiba will be a town like that.

00:05:35.670 --> 00:05:40.420
It doesn't sound like him. He doesn't
have a shred of logic or specificity.

00:05:40.420 --> 00:05:44.420
That's a lot better than
his usual argumentative self.

00:05:44.420 --> 00:05:47.800
Pleasant-sounding words aren't too bad.

00:05:47.800 --> 00:05:52.300
There are loads of problems,
but they can be resolved.

00:05:52.300 --> 00:05:55.670
There'll be plenty of things to do every day.

00:05:55.670 --> 00:05:58.710
I guarantee that everyone will be busy

00:05:58.710 --> 00:06:04.420
because helping each other
is quite difficult work.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:08.750
However, that's exactly why we,
each candidate, are trying to create

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:14.050
the Akiba Government or
the New Round Table Conference

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:17.630
to help those who try to help each other.

00:06:20.420 --> 00:06:25.800
He's right. No matter who wins,
we will definitely...

00:06:25.800 --> 00:06:30.920
We will definitely be able
to bring a bright future to Akiba.

00:06:30.920 --> 00:06:35.050
The Akiba Government or the Round Table
Conference that will be reborn

00:06:35.050 --> 00:06:38.130
will walk towards a new future.

00:06:38.130 --> 00:06:43.000
Akiba will improve.
It will definitely improve more!

00:06:49.880 --> 00:06:54.710
It looks like Sir Saiguu's letter
and those words by Eins

00:06:54.710 --> 00:06:57.750
captured many People of the Land's hearts.

00:07:01.710 --> 00:07:02.920
Is that...?

00:07:02.920 --> 00:07:05.340
It sounds familiar.

00:07:05.340 --> 00:07:09.250
That's the sound made
by the transport gate opening.

00:07:09.250 --> 00:07:11.050
Could it be...?!

00:07:16.710 --> 00:07:20.500
He really is amazing! Well done, Shiroe!

00:07:20.500 --> 00:07:23.300
He really did it!

00:07:23.300 --> 00:07:29.250
He activated the gate... in order
to call in voters from outside Akiba.

00:07:29.250 --> 00:07:33.500
I-Isn't this what you'd
call an election violation?!

00:07:33.500 --> 00:07:35.750
"Everyone who comes
to the polls on election day

00:07:35.750 --> 00:07:39.800
will be considered Akiba residents."
It's written that way.

00:07:39.800 --> 00:07:43.090
But I hadn't the slightest idea
he would activate it.

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:46.590
Hmph. In Westelande,
we had it restored a while back.

00:07:46.590 --> 00:07:49.550
There was even a time we
invaded Nakasu through the gate

00:07:49.550 --> 00:07:52.960
and easily gained a great victory.

00:07:55.550 --> 00:07:59.590
Shiroe. I brought people who
want to participate from Susukino.

00:07:59.590 --> 00:08:01.340
Thanks. I appreciate it.

00:08:01.340 --> 00:08:04.550
I'm happy to see you! It's been a while!

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:07.710
So you're getting along with Adventurers, huh?

00:08:07.710 --> 00:08:09.840
We have different opinions on some things,

00:08:09.840 --> 00:08:14.590
but this town really is special, so...

00:08:14.590 --> 00:08:18.500
That is right. This town is special.

00:08:18.500 --> 00:08:23.960
Adventurers built it, nurtured it,
and welcomed the People of the Land to it.

00:08:23.960 --> 00:08:28.960
Even a naive, insignificant
Person of the Land like me.

00:08:28.960 --> 00:08:34.710
This town was shining that time.
Even if a shadow sneaks up on it,

00:08:34.710 --> 00:08:39.750
it will be filled with an
even stronger radiance for sure.

00:08:39.750 --> 00:08:43.920
This town holds that power.

00:08:43.920 --> 00:08:46.170
The only thing needed is a blessing.

00:08:46.420 --> 00:08:47.710
"Battle of the Guilds!
After Halloween - Field Day!!"

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:49.880
They are worried because
they do not have a blessing.

00:08:49.880 --> 00:08:55.090
If someone has to express it, then...

00:08:55.090 --> 00:08:56.630
Princess Rayneshia.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:06.090
I will tell them there
are people who root for them.

00:09:06.090 --> 00:09:12.130
I will tell them everyone can root
for this town and everyone in this town.

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:18.590
To those of you who have
never met me, nice to meet you.

00:09:18.590 --> 00:09:22.130
I am Rayneshia El Arte Cowen.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:25.710
I am also a resident of Akiba, just like you.

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:32.090
Akiba, an Adventurers' town,
is a very special place to Yamato.

00:09:32.090 --> 00:09:36.250
This world is full of monsters,
and yet, you are safe in this town.

00:09:36.250 --> 00:09:39.300
That alone shows how valuable this town is.

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:44.840
Born into a noble family, I grew up
without being dragged into that danger.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:49.710
However, during my residency here,
I have become able to understand a little

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:53.000
of what convinced you to take a chance on Akiba.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:59.380
Yes. This town holds the power to make
the People of the Land's wishes come true.

00:09:59.380 --> 00:10:04.000
But on the other hand,
we outsiders are like travelers

00:10:04.000 --> 00:10:07.960
who are borrowing the part
of the garden in this town

00:10:07.960 --> 00:10:10.960
built up by Adventurers.

00:10:10.960 --> 00:10:15.210
We were like that until now, at least.

00:10:15.210 --> 00:10:18.380
Those who stand behind me right now

00:10:18.380 --> 00:10:24.920
and those Adventurers who
are listening to my words here...

00:10:24.920 --> 00:10:30.840
They all willingly offered us
their power and wisdom.

00:10:30.840 --> 00:10:33.710
I had very fortunate encounters and support.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.250
At first, well...

00:10:37.250 --> 00:10:41.340
...there were misunderstandings
and arrogant demands.

00:10:44.590 --> 00:10:51.500
But thanks to the Adventurers giving me
a helping hand, I am here right now.

00:10:53.840 --> 00:10:58.300
We were not just receiving their help, of course.

00:10:58.300 --> 00:11:03.210
There were many things that we,
the People of the Land, could help with.

00:11:03.210 --> 00:11:07.920
It is just natural that we all feel Adventurers
and the People of the Land

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:13.840
are both now precious residents of Akiba.

00:11:13.840 --> 00:11:16.960
Because of that, we have concluded that

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:20.630
as the current Round Table Conference
is formed only by Adventurers,

00:11:20.630 --> 00:11:23.090
its system needs to be reformed.

00:11:23.090 --> 00:11:27.050
In order to equally and
adequately listen to the voices of

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:31.250
Adventurers and the People of the Land,

00:11:31.250 --> 00:11:35.000
the Round Table Conference must change!

00:11:38.300 --> 00:11:40.840
The Round Table Conference
will transition to a new system

00:11:40.840 --> 00:11:43.670
and become the New Round Table Conference.

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:46.340
It's been a year since we came to Theldesia.

00:11:46.340 --> 00:11:49.840
We, the members of the Round Table,
think the time has come

00:11:49.840 --> 00:11:52.420
where we need a down-to-earth organization.

00:11:54.050 --> 00:11:57.500
As the chairperson,
in lieu of Mr. Krusty of D.D.D,

00:11:57.500 --> 00:12:00.880
as you all know,
we'll welcome Princess Rayneshia.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:10.630
Log Horizon,
Crescent Moon Alliance, Radio Market,

00:12:10.630 --> 00:12:15.090
Brigade of the West Wind,
and the Silver Sword will remain with us.

00:12:15.090 --> 00:12:17.500
The Marine Agency and
the Roderick Merchant Guild

00:12:17.500 --> 00:12:21.090
will also continue to be in charge of crafting.

00:12:21.090 --> 00:12:24.590
Shopping Street 8 will change
its name to Commerce Network 8

00:12:24.590 --> 00:12:27.840
and work on stabilizing Eastal's logistics.

00:12:27.840 --> 00:12:32.380
The Black Sword Knights will move
their headquarters, but remain as part of us.

00:12:33.960 --> 00:12:36.630
Also, from the People of the Land side,

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:41.550
we've invited Mr. Regan, Sage of Mirror Lake,
as our technical advisor.

00:12:41.550 --> 00:12:45.050
I can't believe the
Sage of Mirror Lake is in front of us!

00:12:45.050 --> 00:12:47.880
So he really is a big shot.

00:12:47.880 --> 00:12:50.800
Furthermore, with the
purpose of managing the city,

00:12:50.800 --> 00:12:54.460
we've invited Mr. Kinjo,
representing the Kunie Tribe.

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:02.630
We're also entrusting him with the
operation of the inter-city transport gate

00:13:02.630 --> 00:13:08.000
using the magic power obtained
from the termination of the city barrier.

00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:12.090
Let me also note that Mr. Regan
and Mr. Roderick's great efforts

00:13:08.880 --> 00:13:12.090
This is amazing.

00:13:12.090 --> 00:13:15.840
made it possible to reactivate the gate.

00:13:12.500 --> 00:13:15.840
Now it's getting hard to predict.

00:13:17.000 --> 00:13:21.210
Today is a very important day for Akiba,

00:13:21.210 --> 00:13:26.000
and it'll be even more important to Yamato.

00:13:26.000 --> 00:13:28.250
Please make your choice without hesitation.

00:13:28.250 --> 00:13:31.840
Please grab your dream
and fly high into the future!

00:13:31.840 --> 00:13:37.380
No matter the results,
we will continue to root for you!

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:40.670
This will be an important election
that will decide Akiba's future

00:13:40.670 --> 00:13:44.920
as well as predict east
Yamato's future at the same time.

00:13:45.960 --> 00:13:49.840
It might be difficult to choose,
but please do not be afraid.

00:13:49.840 --> 00:13:54.000
Your feelings will decide your future!

00:13:52.100 --> 00:13:55.390
Ballot
Box

00:14:01.880 --> 00:14:05.630
He dropped out? When we haven't
even started counting the votes?

00:14:05.630 --> 00:14:12.050
Does it mean he gave up on founding
the Akiba Government? Why?

00:14:12.050 --> 00:14:17.920
Screw that slit-eyed bastard!
After dragging us all into it...

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:25.170
It seems we turned the
entire town into an enemy.

00:14:25.170 --> 00:14:31.750
I-I-I-I-I do not understand!
Why did we have to fly the white flag?!

00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:34.380
You still do not get it, Malves?

00:14:34.380 --> 00:14:38.380
Now that the gate has been activated,
if I am to support this town,

00:14:38.380 --> 00:14:43.670
you can guess what the Senate will think, right?

00:14:43.670 --> 00:14:45.460
That is...

00:14:45.460 --> 00:14:48.960
To the Senate, the gate is a double-edged sword.

00:14:48.960 --> 00:14:52.750
It is an unparalleled means
for their own invasion,

00:14:52.750 --> 00:14:57.170
however, once their opponent gains it as well...

00:14:57.170 --> 00:15:00.750
That is bad. That is definitely bad.

00:15:00.750 --> 00:15:04.630
My power is still overshadowed by the Senate.

00:15:04.630 --> 00:15:09.090
The Senate connived my coming
to this town precisely on the pretext of

00:15:09.090 --> 00:15:15.090
reducing Eastal's power
without using their own troops.

00:15:15.090 --> 00:15:18.130
But now that the gate has been reactivated,

00:15:18.130 --> 00:15:23.300
the Senate doesn't want you
to further build up your power.

00:15:23.300 --> 00:15:29.550
Right. The Senate and
those connected to it, that is.

00:15:29.550 --> 00:15:33.420
I suppose I cannot stay here any longer.

00:15:33.420 --> 00:15:37.840
At any rate, is this also a scheme
by that sage in a white robe?

00:15:37.840 --> 00:15:40.250
It probably isn't a coincidence.

00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:43.670
The key to activate the gate
is an enormous amount of mana.

00:15:43.670 --> 00:15:47.460
Akiba lost the city barrier
and the Royal Guard system,

00:15:47.460 --> 00:15:52.000
but because of that, a surplus
of mana output was generated.

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:54.880
So he used it to reactivate it, huh?

00:15:54.880 --> 00:16:00.880
He must have known that the
Senate is one of our weak points.

00:16:00.880 --> 00:16:06.960
That's not all. He had a broader
perspective of the entire east Yamato

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:11.170
including the People of the Land from the start.

00:16:11.170 --> 00:16:15.130
That's probably why he could think of it...

00:16:15.130 --> 00:16:20.130
...unlike me, who could only see Akiba.

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:25.300
What a formidable man
despite his gentle appearance.

00:16:25.300 --> 00:16:28.880
You called him "Geki in the East."

00:16:28.880 --> 00:16:35.250
Yes. I wanted him under my power
as your right-hand man, but...

00:16:35.250 --> 00:16:36.550
Eins.

00:16:39.380 --> 00:16:43.250
I am sorry. I made you assume the blame.

00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:48.750
Please, this is beneath you.
It was my own choice, too.

00:16:48.750 --> 00:16:52.920
I am going home to the Lake of Nio.

00:16:52.920 --> 00:16:55.960
Will you come along?

00:16:55.960 --> 00:16:57.170
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.800
Is something wrong?

00:17:03.800 --> 00:17:07.630
Well, you did not look like we won.

00:17:07.630 --> 00:17:10.380
Although we won, it was by a narrow margin.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:14.500
Actually, to tell you the truth,
I didn't care about it.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:15.710
You didn't?

00:17:16.130 --> 00:17:18.800
I wanted us to not lead or lose by too much

00:17:18.800 --> 00:17:22.590
so that the result could satisfy everyone.

00:17:22.590 --> 00:17:27.460
I think we were mostly able to achieve it.

00:17:27.460 --> 00:17:29.210
But...

00:17:29.210 --> 00:17:32.000
You are concerned about Sir Eins?

00:17:32.000 --> 00:17:36.670
I heard he left Akiba. I'm thinking
about going to see him, so...

00:17:36.670 --> 00:17:39.340
You shouldn't.

00:17:39.340 --> 00:17:43.550
You knew it was going
to turn out this way, right?

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:49.590
Yeah, I expected it. Or rather,
I might've been hoping for it.

00:17:49.590 --> 00:17:53.880
If he goes there, for him it'll be... um...

00:17:53.880 --> 00:17:58.090
Either way, if someone's going
to see him, it shouldn't be you.

00:17:58.090 --> 00:18:02.210
You weren't sure what
to say to him anyway, right?

00:18:04.680 --> 00:18:10.440
Near High Coast

00:18:06.840 --> 00:18:12.630
Nio is a nice place. The booze is delicious,
and the girls smell good.

00:18:12.630 --> 00:18:15.210
I will not let you smell them, though.

00:18:16.670 --> 00:18:17.960
Who's there?!

00:18:19.920 --> 00:18:22.750
Don't be so alarmed.

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:26.210
Don't make that face.
I just came to see you off.

00:18:34.300 --> 00:18:38.550
Wow... It is beautiful.

00:18:42.420 --> 00:18:47.800
Ahh... This might be the first time
since I came to this world

00:18:47.800 --> 00:18:50.800
that I have been able to appreciate
the beauty of the blue sea.

00:18:52.920 --> 00:18:56.590
Hey, Eins.

00:18:56.590 --> 00:19:01.300
A good-humored acquaintance of mine once said...

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:06.050
"If they try hard even a little,
they should be praised for their efforts.

00:19:06.050 --> 00:19:10.250
They need a place like that."

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.130
Yeah, he did.

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:18.090
I found it convincing.
It's true if there's a place like that,

00:19:18.090 --> 00:19:21.250
no one will feel depressed.

00:19:21.250 --> 00:19:26.250
Making many places like that
is probably a leader's job.

00:19:30.590 --> 00:19:35.630
I think you're the winner of this fight

00:19:37.250 --> 00:19:40.300
because Honesty members
helped the People of the Land

00:19:40.300 --> 00:19:44.710
and have now earned their gratitude, right?

00:19:44.710 --> 00:19:47.880
They were useless Adventurers in obscurity.

00:19:47.880 --> 00:19:54.050
No other guild was eccentric enough
to take them in besides yours.

00:19:54.050 --> 00:20:01.050
You're the only one who was able
to make the best use of them.

00:20:01.050 --> 00:20:08.090
So you're the winner, Eins. You guys won.

00:20:08.090 --> 00:20:12.210
This fight was worth undertaking. So...

00:20:13.050 --> 00:20:16.300
...these are Shiroe's farewell gifts to you.

00:20:20.590 --> 00:20:22.170
This is...!

00:20:22.170 --> 00:20:24.800
They're valuable in their own ways, right?

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.460
Valuable, you ask?

00:20:26.460 --> 00:20:29.460
This is the paperwork
for the zone contract extrication.

00:20:29.460 --> 00:20:33.340
In addition, this is the card
that allows you to use Kunie's gold.

00:20:33.340 --> 00:20:37.840
There are only three of them
in this world. It truly is treasure.

00:20:37.840 --> 00:20:40.840
I can't accept something with such value.

00:20:40.840 --> 00:20:48.000
Even if you say you can't accept it,
I was just asked to give it to you, so...

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:52.960
I think you should do as you please.
I'll do as I please as well.

00:20:55.710 --> 00:21:00.130
Isaac! Please tell him that I have accepted it

00:21:00.130 --> 00:21:04.340
together with the possible
quest entrusted with me.

00:21:04.340 --> 00:21:10.000
No one lost. Everyone
will be happy from here on.

00:21:10.000 --> 00:21:14.250
So you're a guild master. See you again!

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:24.380
Was it okay to have that
muscle head gorilla go see Eins?

00:21:24.380 --> 00:21:27.090
Well, he was suited for it.

00:21:27.090 --> 00:21:33.300
No matter what words I use,
if I said them now, I would hurt Eins' feelings.

00:21:33.300 --> 00:21:35.420
So Isaac was the perfect person to go.

00:21:35.420 --> 00:21:37.750
Is that so?

00:21:37.750 --> 00:21:42.210
I don't quite understand what
Mr. Geki in the East is thinking.

00:21:42.210 --> 00:21:47.170
Who're you imitating? And stop
calling me such an important-sounding name.

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:50.050
So you must like being
called "my lord" after all, huh?

00:21:50.050 --> 00:21:52.880
I don't have to discuss it now.

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:55.960
By the way, what're you making?

00:21:55.960 --> 00:21:57.670
Something for a play about the West.

00:21:57.670 --> 00:21:58.880
What?

00:22:00.960 --> 00:22:03.880
This feels so pleasant, does it not?

00:22:03.880 --> 00:22:05.340
Yes, Your Majesty.

00:22:05.340 --> 00:22:13.920
In this battle, I feel we
gained more than we lost.

00:22:13.920 --> 00:22:17.750
More than anything,
I gained you, a sworn friend.

00:22:19.420 --> 00:22:22.460
Sir Touri...

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:26.630
I was able to see a lot of smiles
from the plebeians who live there.

00:22:26.630 --> 00:22:30.920
And I was able to meet that man.

00:22:30.920 --> 00:22:36.300
Shiroe. A man worthy
of the name Geki in the East...

00:22:36.300 --> 00:22:39.590
I will see you again someday.

00:24:12.960 --> 00:24:15.750
Our milord Krusty, who
suddenly disappeared on that day,

00:24:15.750 --> 00:24:19.590
is on the Eured Continent,
a place far away from Yamato!

